  "category": "Interventional Pain / Neurosurgery",
  "description": "CMS National Coverage Determination for permanent dorsal column spinal cord stimulation (NCD 160.7). Requires documented chronic intractable pain of neuropathic origin (failed back surgery syndrome or CRPS) >= 6 months, psychological clearance, failure of all standard medical therapy, and a successful preliminary temporary trial with >= 50% pain relief.",
